      <p class="eyebrow-sub">California gas compliance</p>
      <h2>CARB Title 20 + LADBS permitting + BHGS license — California gas appliance regulatory work</h2>
      <p>Pitco gas fryers (Solstice Supreme, SG series, SSH, SFSG, Compa gas, Multi-Battery gas, TorQ/ROV gas) all require gas regulator calibration matched to specific appliance spec. The regulator must match natural-gas-or-propane service, building supply pressure, and appliance modulation range. In California, this work falls under CSLB BHGS license, CARB Title 20 emissions compliance, and LADBS permitting in most commercial install contexts.</p>

      <p>For Solstice Supreme specifically, regulator calibration matters more than on simpler fryer designs because FilterMate oil-temperature stability depends on consistent burner performance across the fryer's modulation range. Regulator drift shows up as oil temperature instability, which translates directly into food quality, cook-time consistency, and in worst cases unsafe food temperatures. Our techs verify regulator calibration on every Pitco gas service call and document verified values in the work order. CARB Title 20 rebate programs through Southern California Edison and LADWP occasionally make high-efficiency retrofits (legacy SG14 → SSH or Solstice Supreme) financially attractive — we can advise on rebate-qualifying configurations during service.</p>

      <p><strong>Our credentials for California gas appliance work:</strong> BHGS Registration #A49573, CSLB C-20 HVAC #1138898, EPA 608 Universal Certification #1346255700410 (for sealed-system work on specialty Pitco accessories). All current and verifiable with the state.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

